{"from": "passage:mk-07-30", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-15-28", "note": "Mark: the healing discovered at home; Matthew: 'her daughter was healed from that hour'."}
{"from": "passage:mk-07-31", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-15-29", "note": "Mark gives the return route through the Decapolis; Matthew simply has Jesus come near the sea."}
{"from": "claim:mk-07-19-all-foods-clean", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-15-11-what-enters-mouth", "note": "Mark 7:19 adds the evangelist's parenthetical 'thus purifying all foods' (declaring all foods clean), which Matthew's parallel teaching lacks."}
{"from": "claim:mk-07-26-syrophoenician-woman", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-15-22-canaanite-woman", "note": "Mark calls her 'a Greek, a Syrophoenician by race'; Matthew calls her 'a Canaanite woman'. Mark also gives the healing at a distance; Matthew reports an immediate healing."}
